    "Star layout assumption: no photograph or clip sees two rooms at once, so nothing measures where one room sits relative to another. Each room is attached to the connector's perimeter, door to door where both sides have a door and wall to wall otherwise. Room shapes and sizes are measured; the arrangement is assumed, and the placements are approximate",
    "Manhattan assumption: walls meet at right angles and are axis aligned after a single global rotation. A curved or 45 degree wall appears as a missing face, not a wrong one",
    "All rooms are reconstructed in one world frame, so stitching placements are the identity"
